<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<sample title="Sensor Zone Visualizer">
	<sdk_desc>Procedural frustum mesh generator for visualizing sensor fields of view with live controls for angles, distance, and color.</sdk_desc>
	<desc>
		<brief>
			<para>This sample demonstrates procedural generation of frustum meshes for visualizing sensor fields of view. Four frustums are placed on a single object, facing <ui>forward</ui>, <ui>back</ui>, <ui>left</ui> and <ui>right</ui>. Each frustum is built as a spherical sector (not a real frustum) with adjustable parameters:</para>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Near/Far distance</strong> - radial distances of the spherical caps</li>
				<li><strong>Left/Right frustum border</strong> - horizontal angle range</li>
				<li><strong>Lower/Upper frustum border</strong> - vertical angle range</li>
				<li><strong>Color</strong> - color of the frustum mesh.</li>
			</ul>
			<para>Move the sliders to rebuild the selected frustum's mesh dynamically.</para>
			<para>Fields of view greater than 180 degrees are supported, so the frustums can visualize sensors ranging from a narrow-angle camera to a hemispherical fisheye.</para> 
		</brief>
		<para>The mesh generation lives in <ui>SensorZoneVisualizer.cpp</ui>; the tabbed parameter panel is built in <ui>SensorZoneVisualizerSample.cpp</ui>.</para>
	</desc>
	<controls>
		<![CDATA[
		<p><b>W,A,S,D</b> - Camera movement</p>
		<p><b>RMB</b> - Camera rotation</p>
		]]>
	</controls>
	<tags>
		<tag>Objects</tag>
		<tag>Visualizer (Visual Debug)</tag>
	</tags>
	<keywords>Sensor Zone,Spherical Sector,Procedural,Mesh,FOV</keywords>
</sample>
